A spaced hyphen spelling an em-dash in a doc comment.
-- hit/doc-comment --
Resolve answers the question the caller asked - not the one it meant.
Admit refuses a run whose host is underprovisioned - which the caller retries.
Split cuts the range at one point - three pieces would be two cuts.
The lock is taken before the check - which is what makes the fast path safe.
-- hit/doc-comment whole --
Every rule it applies is derived:
  - one property per tag - in declaration order
-- pass/doc-comment --
The window is 3 - 5 seconds, and residual = 100 - 30 is subtraction.
Flags reads `a  - b` as one argument.
See https://example.com/a-b-c for the background.
-- pass/doc-comment whole --
Bullets holds the doc-list shapes gofmt formats:

  - the first item
  - the second item
-- fp/doc-comment --
The last index is n - 1, which reads as prose from out here.
